      "writtenOn": "2019-07-19T10:48:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please don\u0027t leave irrelevant generated code in the code base. What do you want to do if any of these exceptions happen ? Having you think about it is the entire reason Java has checked exceptions.\n\nIf IOException or NoSuchAlgorithmException or CertificateException is thrown, you\u0027ll return an uninitialized keystore and crash later. Please use the try{} block with a much smaller scope, only try {} what can throw and behave appropriately in each case. (the try {} blocks at the bottom of this file look fine to me)",
